menu "PlantHub Zigbee"

config PLANTHUB_ZB_ENABLED
    bool "Enable the Zigbee coordinator"
    default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
    default n
    help
        The Zigbee coordinator needs an 802.15.4 radio AND the
        zb_storage/zb_fct partitions that partitions_16m.csv provides.
        Only the esp32c6 has both, which is why this defaults off
        everywhere else: the 4 MB esp32c5 leg has neither the partitions
        nor the app-slot headroom (M6a spec section 2).

config PLANTHUB_ZB_PERMIT_JOIN_S
    int "Permit-join window (seconds)"
    default 180
    range 30 254
    help
        How long the network accepts new devices after the user presses
        Pair. The window is a window, never a mode: it closes on expiry,
        on a successful join, and on reboot. A permanently open network
        lets any device in radio range join.

config PLANTHUB_ZB_COEX_ARBITRATION
    bool "Enable WiFi/802.15.4 coexistence arbitration"
    depends on PLANTHUB_ZB_ENABLED
    default n
    help
        Calls esp_coex_wifi_i154_enable(), which arbitrates the shared
        antenna between WiFi and 802.15.4.

        Defaults OFF because it was measured to cost roughly two thirds of
        the coordinator's beacon reply rate, in every configuration. A
        joining device that does not receive a beacon inside its scan
        window reports MAC_NO_BEACON and gives up, so with arbitration on,
        pairing is unreliable. Measured on this hub with a sniffer probing
        every 5 s over a 180 s permit-join window:

                              arbitration ON   arbitration OFF
          BLE scanning            ~8%               22%
          BLE scan held          ~20%               97%

        esp_coex_preference_set(ESP_COEX_PREFER_BT) does not recover it
        (34%): that API predates 802.15.4 and does not reach its arbiter.
        There is no esp_coex_wifi_i154_disable(), so this cannot be toggled
        for the duration of a window -- it is a boot-time decision.

        Turning it on trades Zigbee pairing for whatever arbitration buys.
        Across the M6b bring-up, WiFi stayed associated and BLE kept
        decoding sensors with it off; if a future soak shows otherwise,
        this switch is how you put it back.

endmenu
